      "message": "Here left shift is missing , please take care of adding them similar to below:\nKernel mux driver code refers bit 0 of control flag for the passive/active cable, similarly others also as per following bit0, 1,,2 3 comments. \n   * Bit 0: Active/Passive cable  * Bit 1: Optical/Non-optical cable\n   * Bit 2: Legacy Thunderbolt adapter  * Bit 3: Active Link Uni-Direction/Bi-Direction\n\ncontrol_flags |\u003d (get_lsrx_comm_capability(port) \u003d\u003d UNIDIR_LSRX_COMM) \u003c\u003c 3;\ncontrol_flags |\u003d (device_resp.tbt_adapter \u003d\u003d TBT_ADAPTER_TBT2_LEGACY) \u003c\u003c 2;\ncontrol_flags |\u003d (cable_resp.tbt_cable \u003d\u003d TBT_CABLE_OPTICAL) \u003c\u003c 1;\n\ncontrol_flags |\u003d cable_resp.tbt_active_passive \u003d\u003d TBT_CABLE_ACTIVE;\n\nProbably add macros for the left shifts and please use macros.\n\n\nIssue: Because of this bug, Mux is programmed link training as bi-directional where as retimer is programmed as uni-directional for MBR cables.",
